{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Runtime-Exceptions","title":"Runtime Exceptions","identifiers":["doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit","doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory","doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables","doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation","doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.cs.disable-executable-page-protection","doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.cs.debugger"]},{"title":"Resource Access","anchor":"Resource-Access","identifiers":["doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.device.audio-input","doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.device.camera","doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.personal-information.location","doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.personal-information.addressbook","doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars","doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.personal-information.photos-library","doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.automation.apple-events"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Hardened Runtime, along with System Integrity Protection (SIP), protects the runtime integrity of your software by preventing certain classes of exploits, like code injection, dynamically linked library (DLL) hijacking, and process memory space tampering. To enable the Hardened Runtime for your app, navigate in Xcode to your target’s Signing & Capabilities information and click the + button. In the window that appears, choose Hardened Runtime.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"media-3330446"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Hardened Runtime doesn’t affect the operation of most apps, but it does disallow certain less common capabilities, like just-in-time (JIT) compilation. If your app relies on a capability that the Hardened Runtime restricts, add an entitlement to disable an individual protection. You add an entitlement by enabling one of the runtime exceptions or access permissions listed in Xcode. Make sure to use only the entitlements that are absolutely necessary for your app’s functionality.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"media-3330445"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You add entitlements only to executables. Shared libraries, frameworks, and in-process plug-ins inherit the entitlements of their host executable.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Due to their privileged position in the system, macOS refuses to load system extensions that use Hardened Runtime exception entitlements.  There’s one exception to this general rule: macOS allows the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" in non-DEXT system extensions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default value of these Boolean entitlements is false. When Xcode signs your code, it includes an entitlement only if the value is true. If you’re manually signing code, follow this convention to ensure maximum compatibility. Don’t include an entitlement if the value is false."}]},{"style":"important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"To upload a macOS app to be notarized, you must enable the Hardened Runtime capability. For more information about notarization, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc://com.apple.security/documentation/Security/notarizing-macos-software-before-distribution","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Important"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"Security"}],"title":"Hardened Runtime"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/technologies","doc://com.apple.security/documentation/Security"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://com.apple.security/documentation/Security/hardened-runtime"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Manage security protections and resource access for your macOS apps."}],"variants":[{"paths":["/documentation/security/hardened-runtime"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]},{"paths":["/documentation/security/hardened-runtime"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"references":{"doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.device.audio-input":{"identifier":"doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.device.audio-input","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value that indicates whether the app may record audio using the built-in microphone and access audio input using Core Audio."}],"title":"Audio Input Entitlement","url":"/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.device.audio-input","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://com.apple.security/documentation/Security/notarizing-macos-software-before-distribution":{"url":"/documentation/security/notarizing-macos-software-before-distribution","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give users even more confidence in your macOS software by submitting it to Apple for notarization."}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Notarizing macOS software before distribution","identifier":"doc://com.apple.security/documentation/Security/notarizing-macos-software-before-distribution"},"doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.automation.apple-events":{"role":"symbol","url":"/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.automation.apple-events","identifier":"doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/BundleResources/Entitlements/com.apple.security.automation.apple-events","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value that indicates whether the app may prompt the user for permission to send Apple events to other apps."}],"type":"topic","title":"Apple Events Entitlement"},"media-3330446":{"identifier":"media-3330446","variants":[{"url":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/56cfc71df9e6bfd2a682fdd556780e09/media-3330446%402x.png","traits":["2x","light"]},{"url":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/5973ade3f4df40d484b2159392cb5a11/media-3330446~dark%402x.png","traits":["2x","dark"]}],"alt":"Screenshot highlighting where to click to add a new capability in Xcode’s Signing & Capabilities tab.","type":"image"},"media-3330445":{"identifier":"media-3330445","type":"image","alt":"Screenshot of Xcode showing some of the entitlements used for exceptions to the Hardened Runtime.","variants":[{"traits":["2x","light"],"url":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/e34650edf88337ff29b74fc8176cfc74/media-3330445%402x.png"},{"url":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/5fbee560bf1b1cc71b9ac1b57d7013b7/media-3330445~dark%402x.png","traits